---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About HowNote — Practical Standards & Engineering Tools"
  description="Learn how HowNote connects engineering calculations, pipe sizes, standards evidence and sourcing checks."
>
  <section class="hero container legal-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">About HowNote</div>
    <h1>From a quick calculation to a safer purchasing decision.</h1>
    <p>HowNote is a practical reference and tools platform for people who need to calculate, convert, compare and verify industrial information before they order or specify a product.</p>
  </section>

  <article class="container prose">
    <h2>What HowNote is building</h2>
    <p>The first HowNote tools focus on pipe and tube: weight calculations, nominal-size references and DN–NPS–A conversion. The longer-term product, HowSpec, will connect standard lookup, standard comparison, product compatibility and purchase notes.</p>

    <h2>Why the evidence labels matter</h2>
    <p>A standard identifier, a manufacturer dimension table and a calculated result are not the same kind of evidence. HowNote labels official metadata, manufacturer references, calculated values and regional aliases separately so users can see where each statement came from.</p>

    <h2>What comes next</h2>
    <p>The project will expand gradually from a small, verified pipe-size subset into more engineering calculators, converters and carefully sourced standards relationships. The goal is not to publish the largest table first. The goal is to make each published page useful, traceable and reusable.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>HowNote principle</strong>
      <p>Find. Compare. Calculate. Decide — with the source and reasoning visible.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
